  (hierarchical_label "GND" (shape input) (at 100.33 96.52 270) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left))
    (uuid "20000009-0005-0000-0000-000000000001")
  )
  (text "POWER SUPPLY DESIGN NOTES:\n\n1. USB-C: 5V input with 500mA polyfuse protection\n   CC1/CC2 5.1k pulldowns = UFP/sink role\n2. Solar: 6V panel via Schottky diode (SS14, Vf=0.45V)\n   Connects to TP4056 VCC along with USB\n3. TP4056: RPROG=2.2k sets 500mA max charge current\n   Includes DW01A + FS8205A protection against\n   overcharge (4.3V), overdischarge (2.4V), overcurrent (3A)\n4. AMS1117-3.3: LDO from VBAT (~3.0-4.2V) to 3.3V\n   Dropout: 1.1V typ @ 1A, sufficient above 3.3+1.1=4.4V...\n   NOTE: At low VBAT the output will droop. Consider\n   TLV1117-3.3 (600mV dropout) for better low-battery operation.\n   C5 (10uF input) and C3 (22uF output) MUST be low-ESR\n   tantalum or aluminium electrolytic caps (not ceramic)\n   — AMS1117 requires ≥22uF with ESR 0.1–0.5Ω to stay stable.\n   C6 (100nF) ceramic bypass cap is also required.\n5. Battery monitor: 100k/100k divider = 0.5x ratio\n   At VBAT=4.2V: ADC sees 2.1V (within 3.3V range)\n   At VBAT=3.0V: ADC sees 1.5V\n6. All ceramic caps — 10uF and 22uF must be X5R/X7R, 10V+\n   (for ceramic bypass; use electrolytic/tantalum for AMS1117)\n7. STM32F407 VBAT pin: connect 1uF ceramic cap to GND\n   — required for RTC/backup domain stability\n\nPOWER BUDGET:\n  STM32F407 active (180MHz): ~100mA\n  ATWINC1500 WiFi TX:        ~350mA (burst, 200ms)\n  ATWINC1500 WiFi active:     ~70mA\n  Sensors (all active):       ~30mA\n  LoRa TX (+14dBm):          ~120mA (burst)\n  RN4870 BLE:                 ~10mA\n  Total average:             ~200mA\n  With 3000mAh LiPo: ~15 hours"
    (at 35.56 107.95 0) (effects (font (size 1.0 1.0)) (justify left))
  )

)
